  "title": "Robo-Advisor vs Financial Advisor: Which Fits You?",
  "metaDescription": "Compare a robo-advisor and a human financial advisor on cost, human contact, services and standard of care, and see which fits your balance and needs.",
  "targetKeyword": "robo advisor vs financial advisor",
  "optionA": "Robo-Advisor",
  "optionB": "Human Financial Advisor",
  "segment": "Choosing a financial advisor",
  "h1": "Robo-Advisor vs Financial Advisor: Which One Fits You?",
  "introText": "Pick a robo-advisor if you want low-cost automated investing for a defined goal and accept little human contact; pick a human adviser if you need advice beyond investing or want a person to talk to. In the guides we publish here, we look at the specific legal duties and disclosure filings behind financial advice rather than sales marketing. At ModernWallet, we evaluate advisor and investing choices through regulatory protections, direct disclosures, and the concrete services you actually receive.\n\nBoth models can provide ongoing portfolio management, but their operational methods and service scopes differ significantly. An automated digital investment program builds and monitors your portfolio through software algorithms based on your questionnaire responses. A human investment adviser conducts direct consultations, reviews your complete financial picture, and can deliver personalized financial planning alongside securities management.",
  "comparisonTable": {
    "rows": [
      {
